### Expected behavior

`get_browser_state` should return a snapshot, or a bounded error, in bounded time. Nodes from one frame should never be attached to parents in another frame.

### Actual behavior

The call never returns. Its worker thread keeps spinning after the client disconnects, and every retry pins another worker thread. In our case four of the daemon's ten worker threads were stuck. `cua-driver stop` printed `Cua Driver daemon did not release socket within 2s` and the process kept running; only SIGTERM stopped it.

**Cause, from reading the code** (`semantic.rs` is identical in 0.34.1, 0.36.0 and current `main`):

1. **Ids collide across processes.** [`compose_accessibility_tree`](https://github.com/trycua/cua/blob/24f6fc04d892468defc1f6efff1db5df91e1c369/libs/cua-driver/rust/crates/cua-driver-core/src/browser/semantic.rs#L520-L528) uses the raw CDP AX `nodeId` as `ax_id`. That id is the renderer's DOM backend node id, which is numbered per process. A main frame and an out-of-process iframe therefore reuse the same ids. On the real page, main-frame ids ran up to 2440 while the iframe processes started again at 1.
2. **Ignored nodes leave dangling parent links.** The same code skips ignored nodes, but their children keep a `parent_ax_id` that no longer exists in their own frame. About a quarter of the nodes on the real page were ignored, which left 141 such links.
3. **Frames are merged without namespacing.** [`SemanticDocument::extend`](https://github.com/trycua/cua/blob/24f6fc04d892468defc1f6efff1db5df91e1c369/libs/cua-driver/rust/crates/cua-driver-core/src/browser/semantic.rs#L183) concatenates the frame documents without making their ids distinct.
4. **The outline walk has no loop guard.** [`with_ancestors`](https://github.com/trycua/cua/blob/24f6fc04d892468defc1f6efff1db5df91e1c369/libs/cua-driver/rust/crates/cua-driver-core/src/browser/semantic.rs#L1109) and [`render_outline`](https://github.com/trycua/cua/blob/24f6fc04d892468defc1f6efff1db5df91e1c369/libs/cua-driver/rust/crates/cua-driver-core/src/browser/semantic.rs#L1131) both look up parents in one `HashMap<&str, usize>` built over every frame, where the last duplicate wins. A dangling parent id can resolve into another frame, so two frames can end up pointing at each other. `with_ancestors` stops when it revisits a node. The depth loop in [`render_outline`](https://github.com/trycua/cua/blob/24f6fc04d892468defc1f6efff1db5df91e1c369/libs/cua-driver/rust/crates/cua-driver-core/src/browser/semantic.rs#L1146-L1157) has no visited check, so it never ends.

Even when there is no cycle, the merge attaches nodes to parents in other frames. In the repro, 404 of the 410 kept nodes resolve their parent in the other frame, so outline indentation can be wrong as well.

### Environment

- Cua component and version: Cua Driver 0.34.1 (`com.trycua.driver`, CuaDriver.app). The same `semantic.rs` ships in 0.36.0 and in `main` at 24f6fc0.
- Operating system and architecture: macOS 26.5.1 (25F80), arm64.
- Browser: Google Chrome 155.0.8059.80, driver-owned isolated profile.

### Evidence

`sample` of the stuck daemon. The production hang and the repro show the same frames at the same offsets:

```text
GetBrowserStateTool::invoke + 112
  BrowserEngine::snapshot_tab_semantic + 11592
    SemanticDocument::page + 2704   -> SipHasher13::write, memcmp      (HashMap<&str,_>::get)
    SemanticDocument::page + 2504   -> RandomState::hash_one           (HashSet<usize>::contains)
    SemanticDocument::page + 2596   -> _platform_memcmp
```

In production, `ps -M` showed four threads at 77–79% CPU, each with about 1,630 minutes of CPU time. Those calls had been abandoned by their clients more than a day earlier, and the tab they read had been closed.

A port of the merge and parent walk, run over raw `Accessibility.getFullAXTree` output from the repro page, reports that 404 nodes have an ancestor walk that never ends. The same check on the real page's current load reports no cycle; that load's iframes were tiny, with 2 and 9 nodes.

### Workaround and additional context

**Workaround:** kill and relaunch the daemon (`cua-driver stop` is not enough), and avoid retrying a `get_browser_state` call that has hung.

**Suggested fixes:**
- Add a visited set to the `render_outline` depth walk, as `with_ancestors` already has. That alone stops the hang.
- Namespace AX ids per frame document, for example in `compose_accessibility_tree` or `extend`, so parent links never resolve across frames. This also fixes the cross-frame mis-parenting.
- Consider running snapshot composition off the async worker, for example with `spawn_blocking` and a deadline or cancellation flag, so an abandoned call cannot pin a worker for good.

**Related:** #3668 (open) binds snapshots to one document but does not touch this path. I found no existing issue for this.

