### Summary

On non-English macOS locales (such as Simplified Chinese zh-Hans), calling `list_windows({"app": "Calculator"})` (or "Safari", "TextEdit", etc.) silently returns an empty array `{"windows": []}`, even though `launch_app` and `list_apps` report the app's `name` in English (`"Calculator"`).

### Reproduction

1. On a macOS host with the system language set to Simplified Chinese (`zh-Hans`), launch Calculator via `cua-driver`:
   `cua-driver call launch_app '{"bundle_id": "com.apple.calculator"}'`
   Observe that the response reports `"name": "Calculator"`, while the window object in `"windows"` has `"app_name": "计算器"`.
2. Call `list_windows` filtering by the English app name `"Calculator"`:
   `cua-driver call list_windows '{"app": "Calculator"}'`
3. Observe that `list_windows` returns `{"windows": []}` instead of matching the Calculator window.

### Expected behavior

`list_windows({"app": "Calculator"})` should return the windows belonging to Calculator regardless of the macOS display language, by matching `app` case-insensitively against the localized window owner name (`kCGWindowOwnerName`, e.g. `"计算器"`), the unlocalized bundle/executable name (`CFBundleName` / `CFBundleExecutable` / `.app` bundle basename, e.g. `"Calculator"`), and `bundleIdentifier` (`"com.apple.calculator"`).

### Actual behavior

`list_windows({"app": "Calculator"})` silently returns an empty list `{"windows": []}` because `CGWindowListCopyWindowInfo` (`kCGWindowOwnerName`) returns the localized application name (`"计算器"` for Calculator, `"文本编辑"` for TextEdit, `"Safari浏览器"` for Safari) and `list_windows` only checks the localized `app_name` and exact `bundle_id`.

### Environment

Cua component and version/commit: cua-driver 0.38.0 (85e2b131) and 0.38.1-nightly.20261105.41967274244
Operating system and architecture: macOS 27.2 (arm64, Apple Silicon), System Language: Simplified Chinese (zh-Hans)
Application/browser/window system/image: macOS WindowServer / Built-in macOS apps (Calculator, TextEdit, Safari, etc.)

### Evidence

```json
