### Expected behavior
A token that `get_window_state` returns resolves against the snapshot it names. If the X11 fallback row is discovery-only, it should carry no `element_token` (and no `actions`).

### Actual behavior
The read returns:

```json
{"degraded": true, "degraded_reason": "x11_property_fallback_partial: AT-SPI was unavailable and Cua Driver only recovered window metadata. ...",
 "element_count": 1, "snapshot_id": "s00000002",
 "elements": [{"element_index": 0, "element_token": "s00000002:0", "role": "window", "actions": ["activate"], "label": "Fallback Input Probe", "depth": 0}]}
```

The next call, `press_key` with `element_token: "s00000002:0"`, exits 1:

```text
invalid_element_token: element_token s00000002:0 is out of range: snapshot s00000002 has no rows (0 element(s)). ...
```

`a` is not delivered. The token-free `b` that follows is delivered (the window's key log reads `READY`, `key=b`). `click` with a fresh fallback token is refused the same way, in background and foreground. On a Tk 8.6 window and on a GTK3 app started with `NO_AT_BRIDGE=1`, the same holds, and the default Markdown read (no `tree_format`) prints the row as `- [0] window "<title>" [actions=[activate]]` with its `snapshot_id`; `<snapshot_id>:0` is refused the same way. Re-reading, as the refusal suggests, returns a new token that fails the same way. An AT-SPI window (GTK3 `Gtk.Entry`) on the same desktop and daemon works: its token's `press_key` with `delivery_mode: "foreground"` is delivered.

Cause, from source at `cua-driver-rs-v0.53.0`: the X11 fallback builds its window node with `element_index: Some(0)` and `identity: None` ([`atspi/mod.rs:895-920`](https://github.com/trycua/cua/blob/aed25e921ff303315d95ea23ea2f853b0fb26998/libs/cua-driver/rust/crates/platform-linux/src/atspi/mod.rs#L895-L920)). The snapshot payload keeps only nodes with both an index and an identity ([`atspi/snapshot.rs:75-80`](https://github.com/trycua/cua/blob/aed25e921ff303315d95ea23ea2f853b0fb26998/libs/cua-driver/rust/crates/platform-linux/src/atspi/snapshot.rs#L75-L80)). But `build_element_entry` adds an `element_token` for any node with an index ([`tools/get_window_state.rs:155-181`](https://github.com/trycua/cua/blob/aed25e921ff303315d95ea23ea2f853b0fb26998/libs/cua-driver/rust/crates/platform-linux/src/tools/get_window_state.rs#L155-L181)), and the fallback's Markdown prints the row as `[0]` ([`atspi/mod.rs:922-925`](https://github.com/trycua/cua/blob/aed25e921ff303315d95ea23ea2f853b0fb26998/libs/cua-driver/rust/crates/platform-linux/src/atspi/mod.rs#L922-L925)), which the `element_token` schema reads as `<snapshot_id>:0`. The two predicates disagree, so the only returned row is not in the snapshot that issued it.

### Environment
Cua component and version/commit: Cua Driver 0.53.0 (`cua-driver-rs-v0.53.0`, release Linux x86_64 binary) and 0.37.0, same result. At `main` `dde4a4b64a49` the files involved are unchanged from 0.53.0, and the 2026-11-18 nightly built from that commit (`0.53.1-nightly.20261118.44236707997`) refuses the same way.
Operating system and architecture: Ubuntu 22.04.5 LTS, x86_64
Application/browser/window system/image: XFCE on Xvfb, X11; `check_permissions` reports `x11: true`, `atspi: true`. Target: a plain Xlib window (above).

### Evidence
Excerpts of the responses are quoted above. The full `calls.json` (argv, stdout, stderr and exit of every call) is available on request.

### Workaround and additional context
Workaround: token-free or pixel `press_key`/`click`.
Related: #3344 had the same symptom from a different cause (application-wide indices against a window-scoped count) and was closed as fixed by #3616. This trigger survives that fix. `unproven_identity_is_discovery_only` (`atspi/snapshot.rs:268-274`) suggests the fallback row is meant to be discovery-only; if so, the projection is what disagrees.

