### Primary area

Cua Driver

### Summary

On Windows, `CuaDriver.createPrivateWorker` opens a visible console window when the host is a GUI application. With an Electron main process as the host, Windows 11 opens a Windows Terminal window (tab title = the `cua-driver.exe` path) in front of the app being automated. It stays open for as long as the worker runs, and closing it kills the worker.

This looks like the same class of problem as #5040 (`EmbeddedCuaDriverHost`), but for the private worker path.

### Where

`libs/cua-driver/rust/crates/cua-driver-sdk/src/worker.rs` spawns the worker with `Command::new(&options.binary_path)` (`__private-worker --generation …`, stdin/stdout piped, `env_clear()`), with no `creation_flags` on Windows. `cua-driver.exe` is a console-subsystem binary, so when the parent has no console Windows allocates a new one. This is still the case on `main` as of 2026-11-18.

### Reproduction

1. `@trycua/cua-driver@0.46.0` (`@trycua/cua-driver-win32-x64-msvc@0.46.0`) and `cua-driver-rs-0.46.0-windows-x86_64.zip` → `cua-driver.exe`.
2. In an Electron main process (any GUI process without a console):

   ```js
